From 57a79413a8308c8a0c16432a319cca00731d5274 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:54:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] llama : add managed lazy reader for on-demand tensor
 loading

Standalone llama_lazy_reader: a fixed-size host arena caches pages of a
lazy tensor (qwen4exp PLE n-gram table), read on demand with pread() and
evicted with a second-chance clock LRU. Rows are dequantized with the
same to_float the get_rows op uses, so numerics match the mmap path.

tests/test-lazy-reader.cpp covers page-boundary math, eviction, the
partial final page, single-slot budgets, page-size bumping, threaded
gathers and fd ownership.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
